{
  "schema": "research-public-artifact/v1",
  "concept": "Salesforce single-subscriber durable MongoDB alert distribution",
  "slug": "salesforce-single-subscriber-durable-mongodb-alert-distribution",
  "canonical_concept_id": "concept:6b39dd09c9869078983cc22b6b22325eff82d5a0bd79c8b77bfe51c7ed828027",
  "canonical_artifact_sha256": "f9a44bcf8f5923d8fbb23e01583e58c25313c180a6be0ec23d8a1f8e8585bc2f",
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "clm:0bc3f05033bea73ac2273ce2af299f7efa372ceb2dc70fa5a4bdd25197b0d6d8",
      "text": "Replay position is not a universal event deduplication key: Salesforce says replay IDs can repeat during maintenance. Its event id identifies platform events, but that field is absent on change events. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/event-message-durability.html",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:fb85a30adf68a84ad84d531e6a84e5a93d1073ddc472ec060ed2d2ff13cbb402"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:555e469f38391c7c8949c3f6625aa9584a7072a5f1efa246f908f5b743ea1786",
      "text": "For proposed per-instance fanout, each application instance can open its own collection change stream and serve its connected clients. Budget database connections for those watchers: each active stream holds a connection while waiting, and exceeding the connection pool can cause notification latency. This proposal does not establish competing-consumer or per-client delivery acknowledgments. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/changestreams/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:2c369c031d4b178febd388e24dbdf5f0a40363c0ffe668d3be034a25f917f7b6",
        "ev:5f8aa185e6db3c7714b4b90bbbe94cc873a1d479fc75a3eb0355e817b0584462",
        "ev:a06139d471e60f1050c0583a3babde9ea609eb8b61c734a426e6be999b4e8058"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:c5a93dd39375de49752cbeb3757ee62ffc63c0999ba6f98115e97af8b81a87bf",
      "text": "Avoid opening an independent MongoDB change stream for every browser session without capacity planning. Each active stream holds a connection while waiting, and exceeding the connection pool can add notification latency. Sharing streams through application distributors is a design inference. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/changestreams/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:2c369c031d4b178febd388e24dbdf5f0a40363c0ffe668d3be034a25f917f7b6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:14906ce99241e1a8551d81aa3cb9d461cf41f16d2d8dea3afb5e9f6cf4c0c3a9",
      "text": "Design inference: when the inbox record and ingest checkpoint occupy separate MongoDB documents, commit them together in a transaction with suitable read and write concerns. Advance the checkpoint only after durable acceptance, so a restart cannot skip work that existed only in memory. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/transactions.md",
      "also": [
        "https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/change-streams/change-streams.md",
        "https://github.com/meyc-v1/wolverinefxcontrib-salesforcepubsub"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:004753eeb81460a2b9ccaeb995e4fef1664cbcbb2deaf26d321a68edc37d5338",
        "ev:067e39fb3b8a03febf9a579a84779e60fc679c87809657523e1cb356fff33873",
        "ev:6db17bbaf8fcfd0c408b5639232949f1e146e62780012fb5dd97f1453646e6bb"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:d4a28b601d1a8cfb8a4d1811768a1125d3aa3b4def074e8e4aece93146073fc6",
      "text": "A MongoDB resume token cannot recover changes after its required oplog history has disappeared. Therefore treat change streams as a live notification mechanism and retain queryable alert records for application recovery beyond that history window; this retention recommendation is a design inference. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/changestreams/",
      "also": [
        "https://github.com/mongodb/mongo/blob/master/docs/change_streams.md",
        "https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/change-streams/change-streams.md"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:888d43ad978093f07a2d29fb4ca313c3e4810b062792588941b2068b2e4d7714",
        "ev:b0b6d4c8d2fa1b686bb51bd0574d3717df4a2dd9cbcfea485041e6be890e013c"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:862add4950ecbccc39b3694e13c807c2404553c171df6b46aeca1f94946a1957",
      "text": "Automatic driver recovery does not replace application recovery: the MongoDB specification requires one resume attempt after a resumable error, while the manual says a driver throws if it cannot find a node with the correct read preference. (high confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/change-streams/change-streams.md",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/changestreams/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:4e92efa460ee681e4ad163f51c0c11589a0143f3c62408a0d9a0ec5a37189ef7",
        "ev:b610895121fce1ab7cc743c797ac303c8c597e18ac71dc2d28c71fb186b2c14d"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:0e42c3654d321da665bccfb876db5d54d589de1422f4af9c0a33bf88baefd571",
      "text": "Proposed collector backpressure: request Salesforce events according to durable MongoDB commit throughput and bound in-flight work. Subscribe supports pull-based flow control based on processing speed; MongoDB transactions commit results or end on error. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/references/methods/subscribe-rpc.html",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/transactions.md"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:3b332bfbd3883385a2391043d91b9141a148fc7ad868c97caeb59f03d38ce03d",
        "ev:67004842ac05514dae3d1f7bbc5a58d17fb277b256fe4dbbaf6e317f9673456f"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:d85f349720651a9452a351e1c2954a34bcfa4fc8f52677309c810ae3bd084b79",
      "text": "Salesforce CUSTOM replay resumes after the supplied position. Store replay IDs as opaque bytes rather than incrementing them or assuming they are numeric. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/references/methods/subscribe-rpc.html",
      "also": [
        "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/event-message-durability.html"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:15c6a156d12b27a3d0a3aff8ce446eef480235eb789698565dbc80f200b96797",
        "ev:8cbedad7368e944f052ec5618dedea9ea9fa74e34d2ad48af0298b2290781203"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:90f85aaf3e37e66e1ee65f82bca75368ad5ea43b672305b0aa2fcc1f8d4903d4",
      "text": "Design inference: use one upstream Salesforce subscription to ingest into a persistent MongoDB inbox, then let application distributors read committed database changes. The cited APIs provide the building blocks; they do not certify this combined architecture or require a single subscriber. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/references/methods/subscribe-rpc.html",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/changestreams/",
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/transactions.md"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:004753eeb81460a2b9ccaeb995e4fef1664cbcbb2deaf26d321a68edc37d5338",
        "ev:8acbc4c833569b38d1f134fc14891f56148024a64fc9bcaeda443bb7700ad44b",
        "ev:8cbedad7368e944f052ec5618dedea9ea9fa74e34d2ad48af0298b2290781203"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:da552be99fa8ed2e48abdca00e4358c5884d2e312d7de81738db07430432617c",
      "text": "Salesforce retains platform and change-data-capture events for 72 hours. Use replay for temporary disconnect recovery; it does not provide an unlimited downstream alert archive. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-11-12)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/event-message-durability.html",
      "also": [
        "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/references/methods/subscribe-rpc.html"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:5ec948f6f071f6d6662dacdb7fc9562ac46c0455c7c534800bdf0fffcf3f938e"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:5bb430d4bd359b4beccf4b85e8872dd978f38ca206c92b067c6a2a147d51b276",
      "text": "MongoDB change streams notify only after changes have persisted to a majority of data-bearing replica-set members; this database durability boundary does not itself acknowledge application processing. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/changestreams/",
      "also": [
        "https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/change-streams/change-streams.md"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:067e39fb3b8a03febf9a579a84779e60fc679c87809657523e1cb356fff33873",
        "ev:86b2028a093cf87c18bc409f60d0111e0c2d818373bf05a3080bf6ed9d1cb363"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:e63ec4b30cd10992aecb2fd6f4c66319f5845e3c12cb0050bd15517846d91294",
      "text": "Application processing must tolerate redelivery. The MongoDB driver specification assigns idempotency to the application; the Wolverine Salesforce transport illustrates a durable inbox that persists before processing and deduplicates by event identity. Its example is platform-event-specific and is not proof of a MongoDB or Case CDC implementation. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/change-streams/change-streams.md",
      "also": [
        "https://github.com/meyc-v1/wolverinefxcontrib-salesforcepubsub"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:067e39fb3b8a03febf9a579a84779e60fc679c87809657523e1cb356fff33873",
        "ev:07cd1659921f014a0aa87ee297353bf80cc3c1918838b6f8d2d83dbc519a2aab",
        "ev:e45fc748edeba2a8cff39b89f6e6e46e9f698ebc99768b45172d3ba33d43d6bf"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:4434205250cea604b1d659da2e0aff506c6ab63858e04601e82f7b01b7eef05a",
      "text": "Resume a MongoDB change stream with the pipeline and options that produced its token. Changing the filter can exclude the resume event and prevent recovery. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://github.com/mongodb/mongo/blob/master/docs/change_streams.md",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/changestreams/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:76106c739d26992923ee008acf85af5a2e83278c41abf077ab1dfa7f8ca2686c",
        "ev:888d43ad978093f07a2d29fb4ca313c3e4810b062792588941b2068b2e4d7714",
        "ev:e7900ed19116b432ceee084d0d33b62f1cfcf39b7ee1784d949a5db9154d388a"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:d5af3727cf0d0bab1be8557728ad91d4847650a58cfb9d4571138a9d91d49545",
      "text": "Proposed distribution pattern: use one Salesforce collector to persist alert records and its processed-event checkpoint in one MongoDB transaction; downstream application instances consume MongoDB notifications. This combines documented primitives and is an architectural recommendation, not a vendor-provided end-to-end exactly-once guarantee. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/event-message-durability.html",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/transactions.md",
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/changestreams/"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:8acbc4c833569b38d1f134fc14891f56148024a64fc9bcaeda443bb7700ad44b",
        "ev:c8379a033c364c21706a9faca31bf78b59680553c1a9930eca8db1c70010c865",
        "ev:e09fdfc056aba28d5b261745e46336f13e0048e5fbbfa8884134a31855e9604f"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:22e2ea07097a418e25d032cffedff5cc364c76d17b6200445977ce97abb9f22c",
      "text": "Keep durable alert documents as the recovery source and use change streams to wake downstream readers: MongoDB describes notification services as a change-stream use case and emits notifications only after majority persistence. This is a proposed alert-distribution design. (low confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/changestreams/",
      "also": [],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:2be732a867e0374d2d332b490601736a53ac4f5c40c885217fe74c3b90cc8ec7",
        "ev:86b2028a093cf87c18bc409f60d0111e0c2d818373bf05a3080bf6ed9d1cb363"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "clm:55320a8f1c5b95be2af53f2dd9b8720c9583de312db1cb77be63133684b90a08",
      "text": "Persist alert effects before advancing the processed Salesforce checkpoint. If a crash leaves the checkpoint behind, replay may repeat work; make alert creation and downstream effects idempotent. This ordering is a design inference from Salesforce processed-event replay and MongoDB transaction and consumer guidance. (medium confidence)",
      "source_url": "https://developer.salesforce.com/docs/platform/pub-sub-api/guide/event-message-durability.html",
      "also": [
        "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/core/transactions.md",
        "https://github.com/mongodb/specifications/blob/master/source/change-streams/change-streams.md"
      ],
      "validation_status": "SUPPORTED",
      "evidence_ids": [
        "ev:067e39fb3b8a03febf9a579a84779e60fc679c87809657523e1cb356fff33873",
        "ev:c8379a033c364c21706a9faca31bf78b59680553c1a9930eca8db1c70010c865",
        "ev:e09fdfc056aba28d5b261745e46336f13e0048e5fbbfa8884134a31855e9604f"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "narrative": [
    {
      "assertionId": "prose:bd3ae58d9384eee2bd5e1cb54e08523cd5b3bb50afa7fbe2750bd96f5bce8a5f",
